      "type": "brief",
      "date": "2026-04-25T19:56:18.000Z",
      "title": "MD, CEO & Executive Director exercised options to buy ₹292m worth of stock.",
      "body": "On the 17th of April, Sandeep Bakhshi exercised options to buy 220k shares at a strike price of around ₹221, costing a total of ₹49m. This transaction amounted to 22% of their direct individual holding at the time of the trade. Since December 2025, Sandeep's direct individual holding has increased from 816.30k shares to 1.20m. Company insiders have collectively bought ₹131m more than they sold, via options and on-market transactions, in the last 12 months.",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "BriefActivity"
    },
    {
      "id": "a9aa0888-b415-42d4-a1cc-2cbb2980f1ee",
      "type": "brief",
      "date": "2026-04-19T21:44:50.000Z",
      "title": "Full year 2026 earnings released: EPS: ₹75.89 (vs ₹72.41 in FY 2025)",
      "body": "Full year 2026 results: EPS: ₹75.89 (up from ₹72.41 in FY 2025). Revenue: ₹2.17t (up 19% from FY 2025). Net income: ₹542.1b (up 6.2% from FY 2025). Profit margin: 25% (down from 28% in FY 2025). The decrease in margin was driven by higher expenses. Revenue is expected to decline by 15% p.a. on average during the next 3 years, while revenues in the Banks industry in India are expected to grow by 2.9%. Over the last 3 years on average, earnings per share has increased by 13% per year whereas the company’s share price has increased by 15% per year.",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "BriefActivity"
